1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,836
When you first taught me
about breaking ball

2
00:00:02,836 --> 00:00:04,170
I honestly thought to myself

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,839
that I don't really need
stuffs like that.

4
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:08,425
I was confident with
my fastballs.

5
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:10,122
You were really full
of yourself.

6
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:11,219
Right.

7
00:00:11,219 --> 00:00:12,262
I was full of it.

8
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,097
But now

9
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:17,058
I'm not sure what I would
have done without it.

10
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:18,559
True.

11
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:21,396
Life works
just like baseball, you know?

12
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,356
Fast ball isn't everything.

13
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:24,774
When the ball's fast

14
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,562
it's easier to allow
a home run.

15
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:28,825
You should know how to curve
like a curve ball.

16
00:00:32,156 --> 00:00:33,156
What's the matter?

17
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:34,451
I should tell you this.

18
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:36,368
What?

19
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:37,746
All breaking balls

20
00:00:37,954 --> 00:00:39,456
can work only if
there is a fast ball.

21
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:40,873
What?

22
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:08,526
You caught me when I was
about to give up.

23
00:01:09,652 --> 00:01:10,652
Thank you.

24
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:13,530
I'll catch you
and all the balls.

25
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:15,364
I'm the catcher, you know.
